Here are two free drop-in options in Halton Hills for a toddler. Everything below comes from the operators' own pages, and I haven't visited either place.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Kids & Me drop-in neighbourhood group, Halton Hills Public Library, Acton Branch",
      "age_fit": "families with babies or children up to 6 years of age",
      "when": "Thursdays 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.; follows the school calendar, closed Dec/Jan holidays and statutory holidays",
      "price": "Free, no registration required",
      "source_name": "Halton Region"
    },
    {
      "name": "EarlyON Child and Family Centres, Links2Care (Acton and Georgetown)",
      "age_fit": "children from birth to their 6th birthday, with a parent or caregiver",
      "price": "FREE programs",
      "source_name": "Links2Care"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **Kids & Me:** Halton Region's page gives the Acton Branch day and time. Its page also lists two other Kids & Me sites, Viola Desmond MCRC and Kerr Street Mission, which I did not confirm are in Halton Hills.
- **Links2Care EarlyON:** their Halton Hills page describes in-person drop-in programs, but the day-by-day schedule did not come through in what I read. I left the day and time out rather than guess.

I left out Halton Hills Gymnastics Centre's Pre-school Drop-in (under 4, Tuesdays and Thursdays 9:30 am to 12:00 pm) because it costs $15 per family, so it isn't free.
